(654827, 66970, 17851, '<td valign="top">Great photo! its also my fav. from this challenge</td>', 'Great photo! its also my fav. from this challenge', '2004-04-05 20:55:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(654838, 67133, 4285, '<td valign="top">If anyone was wondering, it''s one of those desk gadgets. My brother-in-law collects stuff like that and he lent it to me. Thanks Tom!!<br/> <br/>The setup was fairly simple. Flash bounced off the ceiling to get the stop motion and ambient room light to capture the movement. Post editting included levels using all 3 eye droppers til I got the look I wanted. USM 125%, 1.5 rad, and 1 threshold. Cropped in portrait orientation. Re-sized.<br/> <br/>A couple of things I would have done in hindsight ( and pointed out by several people - thanks for the contructive crits ) - I would have included the lower ball in the shot and I would have had a solid black BG (setup was too close to the backdrop).<br/> <br/>Thanks again for the votes and the great comments!!</td>', 'If anyone was wondering, it''s one of those desk gadgets. My brother-in-law collects stuff like that and he lent it to me. Thanks Tom!! The setup was fairly simple. Flash bounced off the ceiling to get the stop motion and ambient room light to capture the movement. Post editting included levels using all 3 eye droppers til I got the look I wanted. USM 125%, 1.5 rad, and 1 threshold. Cropped in portrait orientation. Re-sized. A couple of things I would have done in hindsight ( and pointed out by several people - thanks for the contructive crits ) - I would have included the lower ball in the shot and I would have had a solid black BG (setup was too close to the backdrop). Thanks again for the votes and the great comments!!', '2004-04-05 21:05:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(654882, 66425, 4482, '<td valign="top">Man! This was my fav!! I like everything about it!!! You''ve been jipped!  :-)</td>', 'Man! This was my fav!! I like everything about it!!! You''ve been jipped!  :-)', '2004-04-05 21:40:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(654951, 67049, 2700, '<td valign="top">you deserve top 10. <br/>Forget the people who say a tighter crop... if you do that you wouldn''t see the rock... thats what makes this picture apealing to me, contrast and the stark transition from rock to running water to rock...</td>', 'you deserve top 10. Forget the people who say a tighter crop... if you do that you wouldn''t see the rock... thats what makes this picture apealing to me, contrast and the stark transition from rock to running water to rock...', '2004-04-05 23:13:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(654961, 67049, 6405, '<td valign="top">Well,when you see a Snapshot of a pet gets more points than a classic waterfall/rocks texture with river leading lines and water at rules of third placed bellow the hill, you get an idea who is voting here !</td>', 'Well,when you see a Snapshot of a pet gets more points than a classic waterfall/rocks texture with river leading lines and water at rules of third placed bellow the hill, you get an idea who is voting here !', '2004-04-05 23:23:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(654975, 67049, 14043, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by pitsaman:</b></div><hr/><i> Well,when you see a Snapshot of a pet gets more points than a classic waterfall/rocks texture with river leading lines and water at rules of third placed bellow the hill, you get an idea who is voting here ! </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Sour grapes indeed.  It really does need to be cropped closer to the falls if you want a better score.  Talk about looking like a snapshot.</td>', 'Originally posted by pitsaman: Well,when you see a Snapshot of a pet gets more points than a classic waterfall/rocks texture with river leading lines and water at rules of third placed bellow the hill, you get an idea who is voting here !   Sour grapes indeed.  It really does need to be cropped closer to the falls if you want a better score.  Talk about looking like a snapshot.', '2004-04-05 23:36:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(655021, 66795, 4494, '<td valign="top">Wow, you "tied" the tripod to the car!??  How''d you do that?  I''m surprised you didn''t get camera shake just from the suspension and bumps in the road, etc.  The timing is perfect with the sun lighting up the front of the tire.   Very cool.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Wow, you "tied" the tripod to the car!??  How''d you do that?  I''m surprised you didn''t get camera shake just from the suspension and bumps in the road, etc.  The timing is perfect with the sun lighting up the front of the tire.   Very cool. ', '2004-04-06 00:27:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(655122, 66449, 16301, '<td valign="top">I''m surprised this didn''t finish in the top ten. I think it shows enough motion to fit the playful situation. I also liked the post editing, it really fits the innocence displayed in the photo. I was one of the few who gave it a 9.<br/> <br/>Great work, good luck in your upcoming challenges...</td>', 'I''m surprised this didn''t finish in the top ten. I think it shows enough motion to fit the playful situation. I also liked the post editing, it really fits the innocence displayed in the photo. I was one of the few who gave it a 9. Great work, good luck in your upcoming challenges...', '2004-04-06 02:31:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(655125, 67133, 7151, '<td valign="top">Nice job!  Glad to see that DReb paying off for you.  :)</td>', 'Nice job!  Glad to see that DReb paying off for you.  :)', '2004-04-06 02:39:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(655143, 67049, 4008, '<td valign="top">Yes, a classic waterfal/rocks texture picture, but also rather boring IMHO.  It looks so static despite the flowing water. I think it is taken too much head on, straight from the front, and the leading lines could be stronger. The flow of water is to the left out of the picture, you really want it to flow out of the front. I would have tried to get a bit closer, just before where those three stones are piled up. And then get closer to the ground. Or even get a bit into the water, still leaving the ground visible on the right of the picture. This might create a more dynamic feeling to it.</td>', 'Yes, a classic waterfal/rocks texture picture, but also rather boring IMHO.  It looks so static despite the flowing water. I think it is taken too much head on, straight from the front, and the leading lines could be stronger. The flow of water is to the left out of the picture, you really want it to flow out of the front. I would have tried to get a bit closer, just before where those three stones are piled up. And then get closer to the ground. Or even get a bit into the water, still leaving the ground visible on the right of the picture. This might create a more dynamic feeling to it.', '2004-04-06 03:29:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(655153, 66449, 6405, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Sonifo:</b></div><hr/><i> Thanks Darcy!  I knew it wouldn''t do well here.  It is way to abstract for the voters.  <br/> <br/>I just can''t believe I got a 2 from pitsman.  Oh well.  <br/> <br/>Thanks again! <br/>Soni </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Even a 10 would not help much,you know math,my comment was that the main point of the photo was a child and motion blur got washed out by overdodging !<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-06 03:13:46.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Sonifo: Thanks Darcy!  I knew it wouldn''t do well here.  It is way to abstract for the voters.   I just can''t believe I got a 2 from pitsman.  Oh well.   Thanks again! Soni  Even a 10 would not help much,you know math,my comment was that the main point of the photo was a child and motion blur got washed out by overdodging !', '2004-04-06 04:10:21.000000', '2004-04-06 04:13:46.000000', 0),
(655182, 66970, 12319, '<td valign="top">Undoubtly the best shot in the "Motion Blur" challenge, a superb example of the challenge requirement. Beautiful colour and light, it has an oil painting come pastel feel about it, very Turneresque. You should put this one up for sale, or at least pass me an A3 printable copy.</td>', 'Undoubtly the best shot in the "Motion Blur" challenge, a superb example of the challenge requirement. Beautiful colour and light, it has an oil painting come pastel feel about it, very Turneresque. You should put this one up for sale, or at least pass me an A3 printable copy.', '2004-04-06 05:50:17.000000', NULL, 0),
