(655278, 66638, 8013, '<td valign="top">Excellent subject!!<br/> <br/>An improvement would be to have a shorter exposure, as has already been suggested.  Nice work anyhow!</td>', 'Excellent subject!! An improvement would be to have a shorter exposure, as has already been suggested.  Nice work anyhow!', '2004-04-06 09:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(655348, 66449, 714, '<td valign="top">I didn''t use dodge on the photo.  I took this in the middle of the day with a slower shutter speed.  It made the shot really really bright.<br/>I just added mainly contrast to give it depth.  I should show you the original when I get time to hunt it down.<br/> <br/>Pitsaman, I wasn''t expecting this to do well either, but a 2 from you is a big surprise.</td>', 'I didn''t use dodge on the photo.  I took this in the middle of the day with a slower shutter speed.  It made the shot really really bright.I just added mainly contrast to give it depth.  I should show you the original when I get time to hunt it down. Pitsaman, I wasn''t expecting this to do well either, but a 2 from you is a big surprise.', '2004-04-06 11:17:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(655568, 67172, 6999, '<td valign="top">I do hope this placing doesn''t stop you submitting here in future - though it''s a clear lesson in what doesn and does not work as far as the mass of dpc voters are concerned :-). I still really like this shot - as i said, it was a clear second place effort for me, and I particularly don''t understand what it is about this that places it so very low in the list, at least compared to a lot of the absolute rubbish that has been rated higher than it.</td>', 'I do hope this placing doesn''t stop you submitting here in future - though it''s a clear lesson in what doesn and does not work as far as the mass of dpc voters are concerned :-). I still really like this shot - as i said, it was a clear second place effort for me, and I particularly don''t understand what it is about this that places it so very low in the list, at least compared to a lot of the absolute rubbish that has been rated higher than it.', '2004-04-06 14:07:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(655619, 66449, 6405, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Sonifo:</b></div><hr/><i> I didn''t use dodge on the photo.  I took this in the middle of the day with a slower shutter speed.  It made the shot really really bright.<br/>I just added mainly contrast to give it depth.  I should show you the original when I get time to hunt it down.<br/> <br/>Pitsaman, I wasn''t expecting this to do well either, but a 2 from you is a big surprise. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Do you do what I do? After every shot I push PREVIEW  than INFO button.Check the exposure mountain on histogram.Move EV + or - and reshot until gets proper on the middle and no overexposed amount.?<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-04-06 16:14:35.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Sonifo: I didn''t use dodge on the photo.  I took this in the middle of the day with a slower shutter speed.  It made the shot really really bright.I just added mainly contrast to give it depth.  I should show you the original when I get time to hunt it down. Pitsaman, I wasn''t expecting this to do well either, but a 2 from you is a big surprise.   Do you do what I do? After every shot I push PREVIEW  than INFO button.Check the exposure mountain on histogram.Move EV + or - and reshot until gets proper on the middle and no overexposed amount.?', '2004-04-06 14:28:05.000000', '2004-04-06 17:14:35.000000', 0),
(655725, 66449, 714, '<td valign="top">I just got the camera so I am just learning how to do that.  Yes, I do do that.<br/> <br/>I took this shot knowing what it was going to look like.  I like the results.  I know it is hard to please everyone and that is ok...but a 2?  I just don''t see a 2 in this shot, but that is ok.  I forgive you. ;-)<br/> <br/>To a photo doesn''t have to look like a beautiful piece of art.  It can be fun, abstract and even downright unexplainable.  <br/> <br/>If I were to change this shot I would have put some flowers in by the side to give it that spring feel like John had mentioned.  <br/> <br/>Lila is going to look back at this shot when she turns 20 or so and see what her favorite thing to do was in the Spring of 2004.</td>', 'I just got the camera so I am just learning how to do that.  Yes, I do do that. I took this shot knowing what it was going to look like.  I like the results.  I know it is hard to please everyone and that is ok...but a 2?  I just don''t see a 2 in this shot, but that is ok.  I forgive you. ;-) To a photo doesn''t have to look like a beautiful piece of art.  It can be fun, abstract and even downright unexplainable.   If I were to change this shot I would have put some flowers in by the side to give it that spring feel like John had mentioned.   Lila is going to look back at this shot when she turns 20 or so and see what her favorite thing to do was in the Spring of 2004.', '2004-04-06 16:33:45.000000', NULL, 0),
